            },
            "type": "Unit"
          },
          {
            "deps": [
              "x",
              "ceiling"
            ],
            "id": "high",
            "node": {
              "code": "RANGE_HIGH",
              "op": "check",
              "site": {
                "ref": "x"
              },
              "test": {
                "le": [
                  {
                    "ref": "x"
                  },
                  {
                    "ref": "ceiling"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "type": "Unit"
          },
          {
            "deps": [
              "x",
              "fee"
            ],
            "id": "total",
            "node": {
              "expr": {
                "add": [
                  {
                    "ref": "x"
                  },
                  {
                    "ref": "fee"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "op": "value"
            },
            "type": "Int64"
          }
        ]
      },
      "non_applicability": "Not applicable when the interval must constrain the fee-adjusted result instead of the original x: with x=10, floor=0, ceiling=10, fee=1, this composition returns 11, while a requirement to keep x+fee within [0,10] would reject it.",
      "relation": "interval_fee",
      "semantics": "For Int64 parameters in the exact order x, floor, ceiling, fee: first check floor <= x, failing with RANGE_LOW at site x if false; next check x <= ceiling, failing with RANGE_HIGH at site x if false; only after both checks pass, evaluate the checked Int64 addition x + fee and return it. Both checks refer to the original x, not the fee-adjusted result. If both range conditions are false, RANGE_LOW takes precedence. Addition uses the existing add expression and its existing checked arithmetic semantics."
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "dependencies": {},
        "identity": "6a1e9b08f0a487c2f9e92a8f9b10efb105e51fc447bf04d06f01eed5ee4058a5",
        "name": "pair_envelope",
        "order": [
